// A banked `~` is paid at its arm's wake by an argument that arrived while
// the arm slept: a write made by a wake in which nothing the arm reads fires.
//
// Command:
//   timeout -s KILL 120 /home/eric/tmp/review-2026-11-16/bin/graphix-fuzz run \
//     design/review-2026-11-16/repro/c-node-mod-bank-paid-at-wake.gx
//
// `trig` fires at c = 1 while the arm runs and `v` is absent: `trig ~ v`
// banks. The arm sleeps from the cycle after c = 1. `v` arrives (42) while
// it sleeps. `c` ends at 5, so in the cycle `on` returns to true nothing
// but `on` fires.
//
// CLAUDE.md: "a wake is a resume, never a rebirth, and fires nothing for
// anyone"; design/organic_firing.md rule 3: "a body that does not run misses
// what fires meanwhile, a value leaving bottom included";
// design/bind_driven_bodies.md §1.5: `~` "gives nothing until an input
// fires". By those the arrival of `v` was missed and `hits` stays 0.
// Observed, both engines: Trace([0:(true, 0) 3:(false, 0) 7:(true, 0)
// 8:(true, 1)]): the sample fires in the wake cycle and `hits <- 1` lands.
//
// `*r <- v` does the same with the write it holds for a reference that had
// not arrived (ConnectDeref's `pending`): replace the arm with
// `*r <- select c { 1 => 99, _ => never() }` over
// `let go = select c { 3 => null, _ => never() }; let r = go ~ &mut x`
// and x becomes 99 the cycle after the wake.
{
  let c = array::iter([0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]);
  let trig = select c { 1 => null, _ => never() };
  let v = never<i64>();
  v <- select c { 3 => 42, _ => never() };
  let is_on = true;
  is_on <- select c { 1 => false, 5 => true, _ => never() };
  let hits = 0;
  select is_on {
    true => hits <- (trig ~ v) ~ hits + 1,
    false => never()
  };
  (is_on, hits)
}
